msgid_plural "{count} hours"
msgstr[0] "{count} hora"
msgstr[1] "{count} horas"

#. Translators: Waiting time in a Spotify quota error. {count} is the number of minutes.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:91
msgid "{count} minute"
msgid_plural "{count} minutes"
msgstr[0] "{count} minuto"
msgstr[1] "{count} minutos"

#. Translators: Waiting time in a Spotify quota error. {hours} and {minutes} already contain their localized number and unit.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:94
msgid "{hours} and {minutes}"
msgstr "{hours} y {minutes}"

#. Translators: Error when Spotify asks the app to delay requests. {seconds} is the waiting time in seconds.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:105
msgid "Spotify asked Luna to wait about {seconds} second before trying again."
msgid_plural ""
"Spotify asked Luna to wait about {seconds} seconds before trying again."
msgstr[0] ""
"Spotify le pidió a Luna que esperara aproximadamente {seconds} segundo antes "
"de volver a intentarlo."
msgstr[1] ""
"Spotify le pidió a Luna que esperara aproximadamente {seconds} segundos "
"antes de volver a intentarlo."

#. Translators: Error when Spotify continues limiting requests without giving a waiting time.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:110
msgid "Spotify is still limiting requests. Wait a moment and try again."
msgstr ""
"Spotify sigue limitando las solicitudes. Espera un momento y vuelve a "
"intentarlo."

#. Translators: Error shown when loading Spotify browsing results or preparing playback fails.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:429
msgid "Spotify authorization expired. Sign in again."
msgstr "La autorización de Spotify ha caducado. Inicia sesión de nuevo."

#. Translators: Error shown when loading Spotify browsing results or preparing playback fails.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:431
msgid ""
"Spotify does not allow this content for this developer app or account. Some "
"playlists and recommendations are restricted."
msgstr ""
"Spotify no permite este contenido para esta aplicación de desarrollador o "
"cuenta. Algunas listas de reproducción y recomendaciones están restringidas."

#. Translators: Error shown when loading Spotify browsing results or preparing playback fails.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:433
msgid "Spotify rate limit reached. Wait a moment and try again."
msgstr ""
"Se ha alcanzado el límite de solicitudes de Spotify. Espera un momento y "
"vuelve a intentarlo."

#. Translators: Error shown when loading Spotify browsing results or preparing playback fails. {code} is the HTTP status code.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:435
msgid "Spotify request failed ({code})."
msgstr "La solicitud a Spotify falló ({code})."

#. Translators: Error shown when loading Spotify browsing results or preparing playback fails.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:437
msgid "Could not reach Spotify. Check your internet connection."
msgstr "No se pudo contactar con Spotify. Comprueba tu conexión a internet."

#. Translators: Error shown when loading Spotify browsing results or preparing playback fails.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:439
msgid "Spotify did not respond in time."
msgstr "Spotify no respondió a tiempo."

#. Translators: Error shown when loading Spotify browsing results or preparing playback fails.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:441
msgid "Spotify refused the playback sign in. Sign in again."
msgstr ""
"Spotify rechazó el inicio de sesión de reproducción. Inicia sesión de nuevo."

#. Translators: Error shown when loading Spotify browsing results or preparing playback fails.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:443
msgid "Spotify could not load this track."
msgstr "Spotify no pudo cargar esta pista."

#. Translators: Error when Spotify audio/network data or protected account files cannot be read or saved.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:445
msgid ""
"Spotify could not read or save required data. Check your connection and "
"available storage, then try again."
msgstr ""
"Spotify no pudo leer o guardar los datos necesarios. Comprueba tu conexión y "
"el espacio de almacenamiento disponible, y vuelve a intentarlo."

#. Translators: Error when an operation outlives its disconnected Spotify session.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:447
msgid "Spotify was disconnected. Sign in again to continue."
msgstr "Se desconectó de Spotify. Inicia sesión de nuevo para continuar."

#. Translators: Error shown when loading Spotify browsing results or preparing playback fails. {reason} is the failure reason returned by the service.
#: Spotify/Catalog.cs:449
msgid "Spotify request failed: {reason}"
msgstr "La solicitud a Spotify falló: {reason}"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the General page inside Audio settings.
#. Translators: Spoken description of the Playback page inside Audio settings.
#. Translators: Spoken description of the General settings page, read when the page is opened.
#. Translators: Spoken description of the Recording settings page, read when the page is opened.
#. Translators: Spoken description of the YouTube download settings page, read when the page is open.
#. Translators: Spoken description of the general YouTube settings page, read when the page is open.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:22 UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:28
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:26
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:44
#: UI/YouTube/DownloadPreferences.cs:56 UI/YouTube/GeneralPreferences.cs:48
msgid ""
"Move through this page with Tab or Shift+Tab. Press F1 while a control is "
"focused to hear what it changes."
msgstr ""
"Desplázate por esta página con Tab o Mayús+Tab. Presiona F1 cuando un "
"control tenga el foco para escuchar qué cambia."

#. Translators: Label of the box holding the seek amount used by the "Custom value" seek step, in seconds.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:28
msgid "Custom seek value (seconds)"
msgstr "Valor de salto personalizado (segundos)"

#. Translators: Label of the box holding how much faster or slower one press of the speed keys makes the file play.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:31
msgid "Speed step"
msgstr "Paso de velocidad"

#. Translators: Label of the box holding how many semitones one press of a pitch key changes the sound.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:34
msgid "Pitch step (semitones)"
msgstr "Paso de tono (semitonos)"

#. Translators: Label of the box holding how much louder or quieter one press of the volume keys makes the sound.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:37
msgid "Volume step"
msgstr "Paso de volumen"

#. Translators: Label of the box holding how far one press moves the sound left or right.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:40
msgid "Pan step (percent)"
msgstr "Paso de balance (porcentaje)"

#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses what the player does when it reaches the end of a file.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:43
msgid "What happens after a file ends?"
msgstr "¿Qué sucede después de que finaliza un archivo?"

#. Translators: One of the things the player can do at the end of a file: play the next one.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:46
msgid "Advance to the next file"
msgstr "Avanzar al siguiente archivo"

#. Translators: One of the things the player can do at the end of a file: play the same one again.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:48
msgid "Loop the file"
msgstr "Repetir el archivo en bucle"

#. Translators: One of the things the player can do at the end of a file: stop there.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:50
msgid "Do nothing"
msgstr "No hacer nada"

#. Translators: Tick box on the Audio General settings page: after the last file, carry on from the first one again.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:52
msgid "Wrap to top for multiple files"
msgstr "Volver al principio al llegar al final de la lista"

#. Translators: Tick box on the Audio General settings page: remember where each file was stopped and start there again.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:54
msgid "Save current position for each file"
msgstr "Guardar la posición actual para cada archivo"

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding the seek amount used by the "Custom value" seek step.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:69
msgid ""
"Enter the number of seconds skipped by the seek shortcuts when Custom value "
"is selected. Positive whole numbers and decimals are accepted; for example, "
"2.5."
msgstr ""
"Introduce el número de segundos que omitirán los atajos de salto cuando se "
"selecciona Valor personalizado. Se aceptan números enteros positivos y "
"decimales; por ejemplo, 2.5."

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding how much one press of the speed keys changes the playing speed.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:72
msgid ""
"Sets how much each Speed Up or Speed Down command changes the playback rate. "
"For example, 0.025 changes 1x speed to 1.025x."
msgstr ""
"Establece cuánto cambia la velocidad de reproducción cada comando de "
"Aumentar o Disminuir velocidad. Por ejemplo, 0.025 cambia la velocidad de 1x "
"a 1.025x."

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding how much one press of the pitch keys raises or lowers a sound.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:75
msgid ""
"Sets how far each Raise Pitch or Lower Pitch command moves. One semitone is "
"the distance between adjacent piano keys; 0.1 semitone is 10 cents. Enter a "
"value from 0.001 to 12."
msgstr ""
"Establece cuánto se desplaza cada comando de Aumentar o Disminuir tono. Un "
"semitono es la distancia entre teclas adyacentes de un piano; 0.1 semitonos "
"equivale a 10 centésimas. Introduce un valor de 0.001 a 12."

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding how much one press of the volume keys changes the loudness.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:78
msgid ""
"Sets the amount added or subtracted by each Volume Up or Volume Down "
"command. Enter a whole number from 1 to 20."
msgstr ""
"Establece la cantidad que se suma o resta con cada comando de Aumentar o "
"Disminuir volumen. Introduce un número entero del 1 al 20."

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding how far one press moves the sound left or right.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:81
msgid ""
"Sets how many percentage points each Pan Left or Pan Right command moves the "
"sound. Enter a whole number from 1 to 100."
msgstr ""
"Establece cuántos puntos porcentuales mueve el sonido cada comando de "
"Balance a la izquierda o Balance a la derecha. Introduce un número entero "
"del 1 al 100."

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses what the player does at the end of a file.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:84
msgid ""
"Choose whether reaching the end starts the next playlist item, repeats the "
"current item, or leaves playback stopped at the end."
msgstr ""
"Elige si al llegar al final se inicia el siguiente elemento de la lista de "
"reproducción, se repite el elemento actual o se detiene la reproducción al "
"final."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that carries on from the first file after the last one.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:87
msgid ""
"With at least two items loaded, Next on the final item returns to the first "
"and Previous on the first returns to the final item. Automatic advance "
"follows the same rule."
msgstr ""
"Con al menos dos elementos cargados, Siguiente en el último elemento vuelve "
"al primero y Anterior en el primero vuelve al último. El avance automático "
"sigue la misma regla."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that remembers where each file was stopped.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:90
msgid ""
"Keeps a separate resume time for every item and returns to that time when "
"the item is opened again during navigation."
msgstr ""
"Mantiene un tiempo de reanudación independiente para cada elemento y vuelve "
"a ese punto cuando el elemento se abre de nuevo durante la navegación."

#. Translators: Error message shown when the speed step was typed as something other than a number above zero.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:98
msgid "Speed step must be a positive number."
msgstr "El paso de velocidad debe ser un número positivo."

#. Translators: Error shown when the pitch step is not a number from 0.001 through 12.
#: UI/Audio/GeneralPreferences.cs:103
msgid "Pitch step must be a number from 0.001 to 12."
msgstr "El paso de tono debe ser un número entre 0.001 y 12."

#. Translators: Tick box that evens out audio loudness and holds back the loudest peaks.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:34
msgid "Enable dynamic normalize and limiter"
msgstr "Activar normalizador dinámico y limitador"

#. Translators: Tick box that plays the left and right audio channels mixed together.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:36
msgid "Play audio as Mono"
msgstr "Reproducir audio en mono"

#. Translators: Label of the duration used to fade audio when playback starts, stops, pauses, or resumes.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:38
msgid "Volume fading interval (milliseconds)"
msgstr "Intervalo de atenuación de volumen (milisegundos)"

#. Translators: Tick box that fades audio down and up around a seek operation.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:42
msgid "Enable volume fading during seeking"
msgstr "Activar la atenuación de volumen durante los saltos"

#. Translators: Label of the duration used to fade audio around a seek operation.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:44
msgid "Seek fading interval (milliseconds)"
msgstr "Intervalo de atenuación de saltos (milisegundos)"

#. Translators: Tick box that fades audio when moving from one file to another.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:48
msgid "Enable volume fading at the start or end of a file"
msgstr "Activar la atenuación de volumen al inicio o al final de un archivo"

#. Translators: Tick box that fades audio when playback is paused or resumed.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:50
msgid "Enable volume fading when pausing or resuming playback"
msgstr "Activar la atenuación de volumen al pausar o reanudar la reproducción"

#. Translators: Label of the list that controls uninterrupted playback between adjacent files.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:52
msgid "Gapless playback mode"
msgstr "Modo de reproducción sin pausas"

#. Translators: Gapless playback is turned off.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:55
msgid "Disabled"
msgstr "Desactivado"

#. Translators: Use gapless playback only when adjacent files have compatible audio formats.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:57
msgid "Compatible files"
msgstr "Archivos compatibles"

#. Translators: Ask the player to preserve gapless playback even when it must adapt differing audio formats.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:59
msgid "Always when possible"
msgstr "Siempre que sea posible"

#. Translators: Checkbox on Audio > Playback that overlaps adjacent audio files. Files with video are excluded.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:61
msgid "Enable cross-fading for audio files"
msgstr "Activar fundido cruzado para archivos de audio"

#. Translators: Label on Audio > Playback for how long two audio files overlap, measured in milliseconds.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:63
msgid "Cross-fading duration (milliseconds)"
msgstr "Duración del fundido cruzado (milisegundos)"

#. Translators: Label on Audio > Playback for the shape of the volume changes during an audio overlap.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:67
msgid "Cross-fading curve"
msgstr "Curva del fundido cruzado"

#. Translators: Cross-fading curve on Audio > Playback that maintains perceived loudness while unrelated sounds overlap.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:70
msgid "Equal-power"
msgstr "Potencia constante"

#. Translators: Cross-fading curve on Audio > Playback that changes the two files' gains at a constant rate.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:72
msgid "Linear"
msgstr "Lineal"

#. Translators: Checkbox on Audio > Playback that also overlaps audio when the user navigates to another file.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:74
msgid "Enable cross-fading during manual navigation"
msgstr "Activar fundido cruzado durante la navegación manual"

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that evens out loudness and holds back loud peaks.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:98
msgid ""
"Evens out changing loudness and restrains the loudest peaks to reduce "
"clipping. Clear this option to hear the source without those filters."
msgstr ""
"Empareja la sonoridad variable y frena los picos más altos para reducir la "
"distorsión. Desmarca esta opción para escuchar la fuente sin esos filtros."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that mixes the left and right channels together.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:101
msgid ""
"Combines the left and right channels into one mono output. Clear this option "
"to preserve the source channel layout."
msgstr ""
"Combina los canales izquierdo y derecho en una sola salida mono. Desmarca "
"esta opción para conservar la distribución de canales original."

#. Translators: Help text for the normal playback fade duration.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:104
msgid ""
"Sets how long playback fades take. Zero disables these fades even when a "
"related option is selected. Seek fading uses its own interval."
msgstr ""
"Establece la duración de las atenuaciones de reproducción. El valor cero "
"desactiva estas atenuaciones aunque esté seleccionada una opción "
"relacionada. La atenuación en saltos utiliza su propio intervalo."

#. Translators: Help text for the option that fades sound around seeking.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:107
msgid ""
"Fades the sound out before moving and back in after playback restarts at the "
"new position."
msgstr ""
"Atenúa el sonido (fade out) antes de desplazarse y lo reactiva (fade in) "
"tras reiniciar la reproducción en la nueva posición."

#. Translators: Help text for the seek fade duration.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:110
msgid ""
"Sets the duration of each fade around a seek, from 1 to 10000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""
"Establece la duración de cada atenuación durante un salto, de 1 a 10000 "
"milisegundos."

#. Translators: Help text for fading between files without mixing the files together.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:113
msgid ""
"Fades out as a file reaches its end and fades in when another file starts, "
"including after manual navigation. This does not mix two files together."
msgstr ""
"Atenúa el sonido al llegar al final de un archivo y lo reactiva al iniciar "
"otro, incluso tras la navegación manual. Esto no mezcla los dos archivos "
"entre sí."

#. Translators: Help text for fading when playback is paused or resumed.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:116
msgid "Fades out before pausing and fades in after playback resumes."
msgstr ""
"Atenúa el sonido antes de pausar y lo reactiva tras reanudar la reproducción."

#. Translators: Help text for gapless playback modes.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:119
msgid ""
"The Compatible files mode preserves the original audio format. Always when "
"possible may adapt later files to the first file's output format. Online "
"streams use gapless playback only when the next stream is ready."
msgstr ""
"El modo Archivos compatibles conserva el formato de audio original. Siempre "
"que sea posible puede adaptar los archivos posteriores al formato de salida "
"del primer archivo. Las transmisiones en línea usan la reproducción sin "
"pausas solo cuando la siguiente transmisión está lista."

#. Translators: Context help for the cross-fading checkbox on Audio > Playback.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:122
msgid ""
"Overlaps the end of one audio file with the beginning of the next. Files "
"containing video are excluded. Cross-fading takes precedence over ordinary "
"file-transition fading and works independently of the gapless setting."
msgstr ""
"Superpone el final de un archivo de audio con el principio del siguiente. "
"Los archivos que contienen vídeo quedan excluidos. El fundido cruzado tiene "
"prioridad sobre la atenuación de transición de archivos ordinaria y funciona "
"de forma independiente a la configuración sin pausas."

#. Translators: Context help for the cross-fading duration on Audio > Playback.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:125
msgid ""
"Sets the overlap from 1 to 30000 milliseconds. The default is 3000. Short "
"files or a stream that is not ready may produce a shorter overlap. Longer "
"overlaps require more decoded audio buffering."
msgstr ""
"Establece la superposición de 1 a 30000 milisegundos. El valor "
"predeterminado es 3000. Los archivos cortos o las transmisiones que no estén "
"listas pueden generar una superposición más corta. Las superposiciones más "
"largas requieren mayor búfer de audio decodificado."

#. Translators: Context help for the cross-fading curve on Audio > Playback.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:128
msgid ""
"Equal-power maintains perceived loudness while the files overlap. Linear "
"changes their gains at a constant rate. Equal-power can produce higher peaks."
msgstr ""
"Potencia constante mantiene la sonoridad percibida mientras los archivos se "
"superponen. Lineal cambia sus ganancias a un ritmo constante. Potencia "
"constante puede producir picos más altos."

#. Translators: Context help for cross-fading during manual navigation on Audio > Playback.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:131
msgid ""
"Also cross-fades when you move to another audio file with navigation "
"commands. This is off by default. Navigation while paused opens the "
"destination without an overlap."
msgstr ""
"También realiza un fundido cruzado al cambiar a otro archivo de audio "
"mediante comandos de navegación. Esta opción está desactivada por defecto. "
"Navegar mientras está en pausa abre el destino sin superposición."

#. Translators: Error shown when the seek fade duration is not a whole number from 1 through 10000.
#: UI/Audio/PlaybackPreferences.cs:175
msgid ""
"Seek fading interval must be a whole number from 1 to 10000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""
"El intervalo de atenuación en saltos debe ser un número entero de 1 a 10000 "
"milisegundos."

