msgid "Show the playing track in the window title"
msgstr "Mostrar la pista en reproducción en el título de la ventana"

#. Translators: Tick box on the General settings page: let a new subtitle line cut off the one still being read.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:67
msgid "Interrupt the current line when a new subtitle appears"
msgstr "Interrumpir la línea actual cuando aparezca un nuevo subtítulo"

#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses how much detail the player speaks.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:69
msgid "Verbosity"
msgstr "Detalle de anuncios"

#. Translators: One of the two amounts of spoken detail: whole, clearly worded messages.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:72
msgid "Beginner"
msgstr "Principiante"

#. Translators: One of the two amounts of spoken detail: short messages for users who know the player well.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:74
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr "Avanzado"

#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses how much of a folder is loaded when one file is opened.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:76
msgid "What would you like to open with files?"
msgstr "¿Qué te gustaría abrir junto con los archivos?"

#. Translators: One way of opening a file: load nothing but that one file.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:80
msgid "Open the file only"
msgstr "Abrir solo el archivo"

#. Translators: One way of opening a file: load every media file sitting in the same folder as well.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:82
msgid "Open the file and the main folder files"
msgstr "Abrir el archivo y los archivos de la carpeta principal"

#. Translators: One way of opening a file: load the media files in its folder and in the folders inside it too.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:84
msgid "Open the file with the main and subfolder files"
msgstr ""
"Abrir el archivo con los archivos de la carpeta principal y subcarpetas"

#. Translators: Button on the General settings page that tells Windows this player can open media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:87
msgid "Register file extensions"
msgstr "Registrar extensiones de archivo"

#. Translators: Button on the General settings page that undoes telling Windows this player can open media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:89
msgid "Unregister file extensions"
msgstr "Desregistrar extensiones de archivo"

#. Translators: Title of the message shown once Windows has been told this player can open media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:92
msgid "Registration"
msgstr "Registro"

#. Translators: Message shown once Windows has been told this player can open media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:94
msgid "File extensions registered successfully."
msgstr "Extensiones de archivo registradas con éxito."

#. Translators: Title of the message shown when Windows could not be told this player can open media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:96
msgid "Registration Error"
msgstr "Error de registro"

#. Translators: Message shown when Windows could not be told this player can open media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:98
msgid "Could not register file extensions."
msgstr "No se pudieron registrar las extensiones de archivo."

#. Translators: Title of the message shown once this player has stopped being offered for media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:101
msgid "Unregister"
msgstr "Desregistrar"

#. Translators: Message shown once this player has stopped being offered for media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:103
msgid "File extensions unregistered successfully."
msgstr "Extensiones de archivo desregistradas con éxito."

#. Translators: Title of the message shown when this player could not stop being offered for media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:105
msgid "Unregister Error"
msgstr "Error al desregistrar"

#. Translators: Message shown when this player could not stop being offered for media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:107
msgid "Could not unregister file extensions."
msgstr "No se pudieron desregistrar las extensiones de archivo."

#. Translators: Help text for the language list, spoken when the user asks for help on it.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:132
msgid ""
"Choose System default to follow the Windows display language, or select a "
"language included with Luna. A different choice takes effect after Luna "
"restarts."
msgstr ""
"Elige Predeterminado del sistema para usar el idioma de Windows o selecciona "
"un idioma incluido en Luna. Un cambio diferente surtirá efecto tras "
"reiniciar Luna."

#. Translators: Help text for the theme list, spoken when the user asks for help on it.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:136
msgid ""
"Chooses whether Luna uses a light or dark appearance. System default follows "
"the light or dark setting in Windows. A Windows high-contrast theme is "
"always followed whatever is chosen here. A different choice takes effect "
"after Luna restarts."
msgstr ""
"Elige si Luna utiliza una apariencia clara u oscura. El valor predeterminado "
"del sistema sigue la configuración clara u oscura de Windows. El tema de "
"alto contraste de Windows se respeta siempre, independientemente de lo que "
"se elija aquí. Un cambio de opción surtirá efecto tras reiniciar Luna."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that starts again where playing stopped last time.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:141
msgid ""
"Saves the active item and its playback time when Luna exits, then resumes "
"there on the next launch. Clear this option to start without restoring the "
"previous session."
msgstr ""
"Guarda el elemento activo y su tiempo de reproducción al salir de Luna, y "
"reanuda en ese punto en el siguiente inicio. Desmarca esta opción para "
"iniciar sin restaurar la sesión anterior."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that says the name of each file as the user moves through the list.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:145
msgid ""
"Announces each newly selected item when you use Previous or Next, so you do "
"not need to request its name separately."
msgstr ""
"Anuncia cada elemento recién seleccionado al usar Anterior o Siguiente, para "
"que no tengas que consultar su nombre por separado."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that looks for a newer version of the player when it starts.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:148
msgid ""
"Checks for a newer Luna release in the background after startup. A prompt "
"appears only when a newer package is ready to download."
msgstr ""
"Busca una versión más reciente de Luna en segundo plano tras el inicio. Solo "
"aparecerá un aviso cuando haya un nuevo paquete listo para descargar."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that keeps changes such as volume and speed when the player closes.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:151
msgid ""
"Writes changes made during the session when Luna exits, including volume and "
"speed. Clear this option if those changes should last only until the window "
"closes."
msgstr ""
"Guarda los cambios realizados durante la sesión al salir de Luna, incluidos "
"el volumen y la velocidad. Desmarca esta opción si deseas que esos cambios "
"duren solo hasta cerrar la ventana."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that chooses whether a file opened from Windows uses the running Luna window.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:155
msgid ""
"When selected, opening a media file from Windows sends it to the Luna window "
"that is already open. Clear this option to open the file in a separate Luna "
"window."
msgstr ""
"Al seleccionar esta opción, abrir un archivo multimedia desde Windows lo "
"envía a la ventana de Luna que ya está abierta. Desmarca esta opción para "
"abrir el archivo en una ventana independiente de Luna."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that keeps the player out of the system's media controls.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:159
msgid ""
"Keeps Luna out of the system media controls and the play, pause and track "
"keys on a keyboard or headset. Enable this if those keys misbehave with your "
"headphones."
msgstr ""
"Mantiene a Luna fuera de los controles de medios del sistema y de las teclas "
"de reproducción, pausa y pista de un teclado o auricular. Activa esto si "
"esas teclas fallan con tus auriculares."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that shows the playing track in the window title.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:163
msgid ""
"Shows the playing track in the window title, marked as paused when it is."
msgstr ""
"Muestra la pista en reproducción en el título de la ventana, marcada como en "
"pausa cuando lo esté."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that lets a new subtitle line cut off the one still being read.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:166
msgid ""
"When reading subtitles aloud, lets a new line stop the one still being "
"spoken so the speech keeps pace with the picture. Leave it off, the default, "
"to hear each line to the end before the next begins."
msgstr ""
"Al leer subtítulos en voz alta, permite que una nueva línea detenga la que "
"aún se está pronunciando para que la lectura siga el ritmo de la imagen. "
"Déjalo desactivado (por defecto) para escuchar cada línea hasta el final "
"antes de que comience la siguiente."

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses how much detail the player speaks.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:170
msgid ""
"Beginner uses complete, explanatory announcements. Advanced keeps "
"confirmations brief for experienced users."
msgstr ""
"Principiante utiliza anuncios completos y explicativos. Avanzado mantiene "
"las confirmaciones breves para usuarios experimentados."

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses how much of a folder is loaded when one file is opened.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:173
msgid ""
"Chooses the playlist Luna builds when Windows opens one media file: only the "
"selected file, all supported media in its folder, or supported media in that "
"folder and every folder below it."
msgstr ""
"Elige la lista de reproducción que Luna crea cuando Windows abre un archivo "
"multimedia: solo el archivo seleccionado, todos los archivos compatibles en "
"su carpeta, o los archivos compatibles en esa carpeta y sus subcarpetas."

#. Translators: Help text for the button that tells Windows this player can open media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:177
msgid ""
"Adds Luna to the Windows list of applications that can open supported media "
"files. Windows may still ask you to choose Luna in Default apps before it "
"becomes the default player."
msgstr ""
"Añade Luna a la lista de aplicaciones de Windows que pueden abrir archivos "
"multimedia compatibles. Es posible que Windows aún te pida elegir Luna en "
"Aplicaciones predeterminadas antes de convertirse en el reproductor "
"predeterminado."

#. Translators: Help text for the button that undoes telling Windows this player can open media files.
#: UI/Preferences/GeneralPreferences.cs:181
msgid ""
"Removes the media-file associations registered by Luna. It does not delete "
"any media or change default-app choices managed separately by Windows."
msgstr ""
"Elimina las asociaciones de archivos multimedia registradas por Luna. No "
"elimina ningún archivo ni cambia la selección de aplicaciones "
"predeterminadas administradas por separado por Windows."

#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses what a recording is saved as.
#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses the file type a downloaded audio track is saved as.
#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses the file type for downloaded YouTube audio.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:53 UI/YouTube/DownloadDialog.cs:83
#: UI/YouTube/DownloadPreferences.cs:93
msgid "Audio format"
msgstr "Formato de audio"

#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses how much room a second of compressed audio may take.
#. Translators: Label for the stream bitrate selector in Spotify Preferences.
#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses the bitrate a downloaded audio track is saved at.
#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses the bitrate for downloaded YouTube audio.
#. Translators: Label of the list that chooses the sound quality a video's audio is played at.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:66
#: UI/Spotify/CredentialsPreferences.cs:26 UI/YouTube/DownloadDialog.cs:88
#: UI/YouTube/DownloadPreferences.cs:107 UI/YouTube/GeneralPreferences.cs:61
msgid "Audio quality"
msgstr "Calidad de audio"

#. Translators: Label of the box holding the folder recordings are saved into.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:69
msgid "Recordings folder"
msgstr "Carpeta de grabaciones"

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses what a recording is saved as.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:89
msgid ""
"WAV preserves the audio without compression and usually produces the largest "
"file. FLAC also preserves it while reducing size. MP3 and AAC trade some "
"detail for much smaller files."
msgstr ""
"WAV conserva el audio sin compresión y suele generar el archivo más grande. "
"FLAC también lo conserva reduciendo el tamaño. MP3 y AAC sacrifican algo de "
"detalle para obtener archivos mucho más pequeños."

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses how many times a second a recording is sampled.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:93
msgid ""
"Controls how many audio samples are stored each second. 44100 Hz suits most "
"recordings. Higher rates use more space; lower rates can reduce speech file "
"sizes."
msgstr ""
"Controla cuántas muestras de audio se guardan cada segundo. 44100 Hz es "
"adecuado para la mayoría de las grabaciones. Las frecuencias más altas usan "
"más espacio; las más bajas pueden reducir el tamaño en grabaciones de voz."

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses whether a recording is mono or stereo.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:96
msgid ""
"Mono stores one channel and is usually enough for a single microphone. "
"Stereo preserves separate left and right channels for music and system audio."
msgstr ""
"Mono guarda un solo canal y suele ser suficiente para un micrófono. Estéreo "
"conserva los canales izquierdo y derecho por separado para música y audio "
"del sistema."

#. Translators: Help text for the list that chooses how much room a second of compressed audio may take.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:99
msgid ""
"For MP3 and AAC, a higher bitrate preserves more detail but creates a larger "
"file. WAV and FLAC do not use this choice."
msgstr ""
"Para MP3 y AAC, una tasa de bits más alta conserva más detalles, pero crea "
"un archivo más grande. WAV y FLAC no utilizan esta opción."

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding the folder recordings are saved into.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:102
msgid ""
"Enter the destination directory. Luna creates it when necessary and gives "
"each recording a timestamped name to prevent accidental replacement."
msgstr ""
"Introduce el directorio de destino. Luna lo creará si es necesario y "
"asignará a cada grabación un nombre con marca de tiempo para evitar "
"sobrescribirla accidentalmente."

#. Translators: Help text for the button that opens a window for choosing the recordings folder.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:105
msgid ""
"Opens a directory picker and puts the selected path in the recordings folder "
"box."
msgstr ""
"Abre un selector de directorios y coloca la ruta seleccionada en la casilla "
"de la carpeta de grabaciones."

#. Translators: Shown when the Recording settings page was left with no folder to save into.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:133
msgid "Choose a folder for recordings."
msgstr "Elige una carpeta para las grabaciones."

#. Translators: Title of the window that asks where recordings should be saved.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:255
#: UI/Recording/RecordingDialog.cs:469
msgid "Select the folder for recordings"
msgstr "Seleccionar la carpeta para las grabaciones"

#. Translators: A sample rate, as shown in a list. {value} is a number such as 44100.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:280
#: UI/Recording/RecordingDialog.cs:713
msgid "{value} Hz"
msgstr "{value} Hz"

#. Translators: A bitrate, as shown in a list. {value} is a number such as 192.
#: UI/Preferences/RecordingPreferences.cs:283
#: UI/Recording/RecordingDialog.cs:716
msgid "{value} kbps"
msgstr "{value} kbps"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the Keyboard shortcuts settings page, read when the page is opened.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:39
msgid ""
"Keyboard shortcuts. Select an action, then edit its primary or secondary "
"local shortcut."
msgstr ""
"Atajos de teclado. Selecciona una acción y edita su atajo local primario o "
"secundario."

#. Translators: Spoken description of the Global shortcuts settings page, read when the page is opened.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:41
msgid ""
"System-wide shortcuts. Select an action, then edit the combination that "
"triggers it from any application."
msgstr ""
"Atajos del sistema. Selecciona una acción y edita la combinación que la "
"activa desde cualquier aplicación."

#. Translators: Heading above the list of shortcuts that work while the player is the program in front.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:51
msgid "Local Shortcuts"
msgstr "Atajos locales"

#. Translators: Heading of the shortcut list column naming each command.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:56
msgid "Action"
msgstr "Acción"

#. Translators: Heading of the shortcut list column holding the first key combination of each command.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:59
msgid "Primary Shortcut"
msgstr "Atajo primario"

#. Translators: Heading of the shortcut list column holding the key combination of each command, on the page
#. where a command has only one.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:62
msgid "Shortcut"
msgstr "Atajo"

#. Translators: Heading of the shortcut list column holding the second, alternative key combination of each command.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:65
msgid "Secondary Shortcut"
msgstr "Atajo secundario"

#. Translators: Button that changes the first key combination of the chosen command.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:68
msgid "Edit Primary Shortcut"
msgstr "Editar atajo primario"

#. Translators: Button that changes the key combination of the chosen command, on the page where a command has only one.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:70
msgid "Edit Shortcut"
msgstr "Editar atajo"

#. Translators: Button that changes the second, alternative key combination of the chosen command.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:72
msgid "Edit Secondary Shortcut"
msgstr "Editar atajo secundario"

#. Translators: Button that puts every shortcut on this page back to the combination the player came with.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:74
msgid "Reset to Defaults"
msgstr "Restablecer a valores predeterminados"

#. Translators: Shown when the combination the user pressed is already used by another command.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:145
msgid "That shortcut is already assigned to another action."
msgstr "Ese atajo ya está asignado a otra acción."

#. Translators: Title of the message shown when the combination pressed is already used by another command.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:147
msgid "Shortcut Conflict"
msgstr "Conflicto de atajos"

#. Translators: Asks the user to confirm putting every shortcut on this page back to the combination the player came with.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:184
msgid "Reset all shortcuts to defaults?"
msgstr "¿Restablecer todos los atajos a los valores predeterminados?"

#. Translators: Title of the window that asks the user to confirm putting every shortcut back as it was.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:186
msgid "Confirm Reset"
msgstr "Confirmar restablecimiento"

#. Translators: Title of the window that waits for a combination that will work while another program is in front.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:272
msgid "Set Global Shortcut"
msgstr "Establecer atajo global"

#. Translators: Title of the small window that waits for the user to press the combination they want.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:274
msgid "Set Shortcut"
msgstr "Establecer atajo"

#. Translators: Message in the window that waits for a system-wide key combination. Escape is the name of the key that closes it.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:277
msgid "Press the desired global shortcut. Escape cancels."
msgstr "Presiona el atajo global deseado. Escape cancela."

#. Translators: Message in the window that waits for a key combination. Escape is the name of the key that closes it.
#: UI/Preferences/ShortcutPreferences.cs:279
msgid "Press the desired shortcut. Escape cancels."
msgstr "Presiona el atajo deseado. Escape cancela."

#. Translators: Spoken description of the box for the shortest silence that will be trimmed, on the silence removal settings page.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:11
msgid ""
"Quiet sections shorter than this many seconds remain unchanged. The default "
"is 0.5 seconds."
msgstr ""
"Las secciones silenciosas más cortas que este número de segundos "
"permanecerán sin cambios. El valor predeterminado es 0.5 segundos."

#. Translators: Spoken description of the box for the loudness under which sound counts as silence, on the silence removal settings page.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:13
msgid ""
"Samples quieter than this decibel level count as silence. Enter a number "
"such as -30."
msgstr ""
"Las muestras más silenciosas que este nivel de decibelios se consideran "
"silencio. Introduce un número como -30."

#. Translators: Spoken description of the list of ways silence can be measured, on the silence removal settings page. Peak and RMS are the names of the two methods.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:15
msgid ""
"Peak follows the loudest sample in each analysis window and reacts to brief "
"sounds. RMS averages the window for steadier detection."
msgstr ""
"Peak sigue la muestra más alta en cada ventana de análisis y reacciona a "
"sonidos breves. RMS promedia la ventana para una detección más estable."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: which section of sound should end trimming at the start of the file.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:20
msgid "Leading silent parts to trim"
msgstr "Partes silenciosas iniciales a recortar"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced setting that chooses which section of sound ends trimming at the start of the file.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:22
msgid ""
"Use 0 to leave the beginning untouched or 1 to remove its initial silence. "
"Higher values continue trimming through additional sections of sound."
msgstr ""
"Usa 0 para no modificar el inicio o 1 para eliminar el silencio inicial. "
"Valores más altos continúan recortando a través de secciones adicionales de "
"sonido."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: how long sound must continue before trimming at the start stops.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:24
msgid "Sound required before leading trim stops (seconds)"
msgstr "Sonido requerido antes de detener el recorte inicial (segundos)"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced setting for how long sound must continue before trimming at the start stops.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:26
msgid ""
"Sound must stay above the threshold for this long before leading-silence "
"trimming stops. The default is 0.2 seconds."
msgstr ""
"El sonido debe mantenerse por encima del umbral durante este tiempo antes de "
"detener el recorte de silencio inicial. El valor predeterminado es 0.2 "
"segundos."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: how many silent parts to cut once the sound has begun.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:28
msgid "Silent parts to trim after audio starts"
msgstr "Partes silenciosas a recortar después de que inicie el audio"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced silence removal setting for how many silent parts to cut once the sound has begun. Minus one means every one of them.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:30
msgid ""
"Use -1 to shorten every qualifying pause after sound begins, or 0 to leave "
"later pauses untouched."
msgstr ""
"Usa -1 para acortar cada pausa apta después de que comience el sonido, o 0 "
"para no modificar las pausas posteriores."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: how long silence in the middle or at the end must be before it is cut.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:32
msgid "Minimum inner silence length (seconds)"
msgstr "Duración mínima del silencio interno (segundos)"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced silence removal setting for how long silence in the middle or at the end must be before it is cut.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:34
msgid ""
"A quiet section after sound begins must last at least this long before it is "
"shortened."
msgstr ""
"Una sección silenciosa después de que comienza el sonido debe durar al menos "
"este tiempo antes de ser acortada."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: how much of a pause to leave where silence was cut.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:36
msgid "Pause to keep after trimmed silence (seconds)"
msgstr "Pausa a conservar tras el silencio recortado (segundos)"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced silence removal setting for how much of a pause to leave where silence was cut.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:38
msgid ""
"Keeps up to this much of a pause instead of removing it completely. The "
"default is 0.2 seconds."
msgstr ""
"Conserva hasta este tiempo de pausa en lugar de eliminarla por completo. El "
"valor predeterminado es 0.2 segundos."

#. Translators: Label of an advanced silence removal setting: the length of sound looked at at once when deciding whether it is silent.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:40
msgid "Detection window size (seconds)"
msgstr "Tamaño de la ventana de detección (segundos)"

#. Translators: Spoken description of the advanced silence removal setting for the length of sound looked at at once when deciding whether it is silent.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:42
msgid ""
"Sets how many seconds of samples are measured together. Larger windows are "
"steadier; smaller windows react faster. The default is 0.02."
msgstr ""
"Establece cuántos segundos de muestras se miden juntos. Ventanas más grandes "
"son más estables; ventanas más pequeñas reaccionan más rápido. El valor "
"predeterminado es 0.02."

#. Translators: Spoken description of the whole silence removal settings page, read when the page is opened.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:57
msgid ""
"The basic controls decide how long and how quiet a pause must be before Luna "
"shortens it. Advanced controls treat silence at the beginning and after "
"sound starts separately."
msgstr ""
"Los controles básicos determinan qué tan larga y silenciosa debe ser una "
"pausa antes de que Luna la acorte. Los controles avanzados tratan por "
"separado el silencio del inicio y el posterior."

#. Translators: Title of the group holding the silence removal settings.
#. "FFmpeg silenceremove" is the name of the filter doing the work and is not translated.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:65
msgid "Silence removal (FFmpeg silenceremove)"
msgstr "Eliminación de silencio (FFmpeg silenceremove)"

#. Translators: Label of the box for the shortest silence that will be trimmed, on the silence removal settings page.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:70
msgid "Minimum silence duration (seconds)"
msgstr "Duración mínima del silencio (segundos)"

#. Translators: Label of the box for the loudness under which sound counts as silence, on the silence removal settings page.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:72
msgid "Silence threshold"
msgstr "Umbral de silencio"

#. Translators: Label of the tick box that shows the rest of the silence removal settings.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:76
msgid "Show advanced settings"
msgstr "Mostrar configuración avanzada"

#. Translators: Label of the list of ways silence can be measured, on the silence removal settings page.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:90
msgid "Detection mode"
msgstr "Modo de detección"

#. Translators: One of the two ways silence can be measured: by the loudest moment. This one answers quickly to speech.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:94
msgid "Peak (fast reaction)"
msgstr "Peak (reacción rápida)"

#. Translators: One of the two ways silence can be measured: by the average loudness. This one is steadier. RMS is the usual name for it and can be left as it is.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:96
msgid "RMS (smoother)"
msgstr "RMS (más suave)"

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding the shortest silence that will be trimmed, spoken when the user asks for help on it.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:116
msgid ""
"Raise this value to preserve more short pauses, or lower it to remove "
"briefer pauses. A quiet section is changed only after it lasts for the "
"entered number of seconds."
msgstr ""
"Aumenta este valor para conservar más pausas cortas, o redúcelo para "
"eliminar pausas más breves. Una sección silenciosa solo se modifica tras "
"durar el número de segundos ingresado."

#. Translators: Help text for the box holding the loudness under which sound counts as silence, spoken when the user asks for help on it.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:120
msgid ""
"Enter a decibel value such as -30. A less negative value treats louder audio "
"as silence and removes more; a more negative value limits removal to very "
"quiet audio."
msgstr ""
"Introduce un valor en decibelios como -30. Un valor menos negativo trata el "
"audio más alto como silencio y elimina más; un valor más negativo limita la "
"eliminación al audio muy silencioso."

#. Translators: Help text for the tick box that shows the rest of the silence removal settings.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:124
msgid ""
"Reveals separate controls for leading and later silence, the amount of each "
"pause to retain, and the method used to measure loudness."
msgstr ""
"Muestra controles independientes para el silencio inicial y posterior, la "
"cantidad de pausa a conservar y el método usado para medir la sonoridad."

#. Translators: Help text for the list of ways silence can be measured. Peak and RMS are the names of the two methods.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:128
msgid ""
"Peak uses the loudest sample in each analysis window and responds to brief "
"sounds. RMS uses average energy, producing a steadier result that is less "
"affected by short spikes."
msgstr ""
"Peak utiliza la muestra más alta en cada ventana de análisis y responde a "
"sonidos breves. RMS utiliza la energía promedio, logrando un resultado más "
"estable y menos afectado por picos cortos."

#. Translators: Error message shown when the shortest silence to trim was typed as something other than a number, or as a negative one.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:138
msgid "Minimum silence duration must be a non-negative number."
msgstr "La duración mínima del silencio debe ser un número no negativo."

#. Translators: Error message shown when the silence loudness threshold was typed as something other than a number.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:144
msgid "Silence threshold must be a valid number."
msgstr "El umbral de silencio debe ser un número válido."

#. Translators: Error message shown when an advanced silence removal setting needs a whole number.
#. {field} is the name of the setting, such as "Leading silent parts to trim".
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:159
msgid "{field} must be an integer value."
msgstr "{field} must be an integer value."

#. Translators: Error message shown when an advanced silence removal setting cannot be negative.
#. {field} is the name of the setting, such as "Leading silent parts to trim".
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:166
msgid "{field} must be zero or greater."
msgstr "{field} must be zero or greater."

#. Translators: Error message shown when an advanced silence removal setting accepts -1 but nothing lower.
#. {field} is the name of the setting, such as "Silent parts to trim after audio starts".
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:173
msgid "{field} must be -1 or greater."
msgstr "{field} must be -1 or greater."

#. Translators: Error message shown when an advanced silence removal setting needs a number that is not negative.
#. {field} is the name of the setting, such as "Sound required before leading trim stops (seconds)".
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:181
msgid "{field} must be a non-negative number."
msgstr "{field} must be a non-negative number."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting that chooses which section of sound ends trimming at the start of the file.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:271
msgid ""
"Use 0 to preserve the beginning or 1 to remove initial silence until "
"sustained sound is found. Values above 1 continue discarding audio through "
"additional non-silent sections."
msgstr ""
"Usa 0 para conservar el inicio o 1 para eliminar el silencio inicial hasta "
"encontrar un sonido sostenido. Los valores superiores a 1 continúan "
"descartando audio a través de secciones adicionales no silenciosas."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting holding how long sound must continue before trimming at the start stops.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:274
msgid ""
"After initial trimming, sound must remain above the threshold for this many "
"seconds before Luna starts keeping it. The default is 0.2."
msgstr ""
"Tras el recorte inicial, el sonido debe permanecer por encima del umbral "
"durante este número de segundos antes de que Luna comience a conservarlo. El "
"valor predeterminado es 0.2."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting holding how many silent parts to cut once the sound has begun.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:277
msgid ""
"Use -1 to shorten every qualifying pause after sound begins. Use 0 to "
"preserve later silence; positive values limit how many sections are removed."
msgstr ""
"Usa -1 para acortar cada pausa apta después de que comience el sonido. Usa 0 "
"para conservar el silencio posterior; los valores positivos limitan cuántas "
"secciones se eliminan."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting holding how long silence in the middle or at the end must be before it is cut.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:279
msgid ""
"A pause after sound begins must remain below the threshold for this many "
"seconds before Luna shortens it."
msgstr ""
"Una pausa después de que comience el sonido debe permanecer por debajo del "
"umbral durante este número de segundos antes de que Luna la acorte."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting holding how much of a pause to leave where silence was cut.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:281
msgid ""
"Enter how many seconds of a removed pause should remain, so words do not run "
"together. The default is 0.2."
msgstr ""
"Introduce cuántos segundos de una pausa eliminada deben conservarse, para "
"que las palabras no se junten. El valor predeterminado es 0.2."

#. Translators: Help text for the advanced setting holding the length of sound looked at at once when deciding whether it is silent.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:283
msgid ""
"Sets the span of audio used for each loudness measurement. Larger values "
"smooth sudden changes; smaller values react faster. The default is 0.02 "
"seconds."
msgstr ""
"Establece el intervalo de audio utilizado para cada medición de sonoridad. "
"Valores más grandes suavizan los cambios abruptos; valores más pequeños "
"reaccionan más rápido. El valor predeterminado es 0.02 segundos."

#. Translators: Help text used for any silence removal setting with no help text of its own.
#: UI/Preferences/SilencePreferences.cs:286
msgid "Enter a numeric value, then press OK to apply it."
msgstr "Introduce un valor numérico y presiona Aceptar para aplicarlo."

